1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:01,239
Last lesson,

2
00:00:01,239 --> 00:00:02,718
the quality gate failed.

3
00:00:02,718 --> 00:00:04,012
And nothing happened.

4
00:00:04,012 --> 00:00:04,936
Nobody stopped.

5
00:00:04,936 --> 00:00:06,537
The code just kept moving.

6
00:00:07,087 --> 00:00:11,951
That is the problem. A gate that only shows red on a dashboard, is a suggestion.

7
00:00:12,501 --> 00:00:14,627
Today we connect it to Jenkins.

8
00:00:14,627 --> 00:00:15,999
When the gate fails,

9
00:00:15,999 --> 00:00:17,097
the build fails.

10
00:00:17,097 --> 00:00:17,782
No deploy.

11
00:00:17,782 --> 00:00:18,537
No release.

12
00:00:18,537 --> 00:00:19,840
The pipeline stops.

13
00:00:20,390 --> 00:00:24,849
We use the official plugin, a webhook, and one line: wait for quality gate.

14
00:00:26,399 --> 00:00:27,828
Here is what to expect.

15
00:00:28,378 --> 00:00:32,346
One: why we use the official Sonar cube plugin, and what it adds.

16
00:00:32,896 --> 00:00:38,059
Two: how Jenkins, the scanner and the server talk to each other. Including the webhook.

17
00:00:38,609 --> 00:00:39,939
Three: a live demo.

18
00:00:39,939 --> 00:00:42,249
We connect Jenkins to Sonar cube,

19
00:00:42,249 --> 00:00:43,370
add the webhook,

20
00:00:43,370 --> 00:00:44,700
and run a pipeline.

21
00:00:44,700 --> 00:00:46,170
It fails at the gate.

22
00:00:46,170 --> 00:00:47,290
We fix the code.

23
00:00:47,290 --> 00:00:48,550
And it goes green.

24
00:00:49,100 --> 00:00:52,386
Four: the mistakes that waste hours, and the lab files.

25
00:00:52,936 --> 00:00:55,965
This is objective six of the Sonar cube domain.

26
00:00:57,515 --> 00:00:58,880
First, why a plugin?

27
00:00:59,430 --> 00:01:02,013
You can already run a scan from Jenkins.

28
00:01:02,013 --> 00:01:03,046
Just call Maven,

29
00:01:03,046 --> 00:01:04,337
with the Sonar goal.

30
00:01:04,337 --> 00:01:06,726
We did that in lesson one fifty-nine.

31
00:01:07,276 --> 00:01:10,178
The official Sonar cube plugin adds three things.

32
00:01:10,728 --> 00:01:16,296
One: a place to register the server, with its address and its token. Once, for every job.

33
00:01:16,846 --> 00:01:19,247
Two: a step called with Sonar cube env.

34
00:01:19,247 --> 00:01:22,018
It gives your scan the address and the token,

35
00:01:22,018 --> 00:01:24,419
without you pasting them in the script.

36
00:01:24,969 --> 00:01:27,593
Three: a step called wait for quality gate.

37
00:01:27,593 --> 00:01:28,996
It pauses the pipeline,

38
00:01:28,996 --> 00:01:30,949
asks the server for the verdict,

39
00:01:30,949 --> 00:01:33,268
and fails the build if the gate fails.

40
00:01:33,818 --> 00:01:38,703
The token stays in the Jenkins credentials. It never appears in your pipeline file.

41
00:01:40,253 --> 00:01:41,640
How do the pieces talk?

42
00:01:42,190 --> 00:01:46,990
Step one: the scan runs inside the build, and uploads its report to the server.

43
00:01:47,540 --> 00:01:50,513
Step two: the server does not answer right away.

44
00:01:50,513 --> 00:01:53,052
It analyses the report in the background.

45
00:01:53,052 --> 00:01:54,601
This takes a few seconds.

46
00:01:55,151 --> 00:01:57,081
Step three: when it is finished,

47
00:01:57,081 --> 00:01:59,615
the server calls a web address on Jenkins.

48
00:01:59,615 --> 00:02:01,123
That call is the webhook.

49
00:02:01,123 --> 00:02:02,511
It carries the verdict.

50
00:02:03,061 --> 00:02:05,472
Step four: the wait step receives it.

51
00:02:05,472 --> 00:02:05,928
Passed,

52
00:02:05,928 --> 00:02:07,296
the pipeline goes on.

53
00:02:07,296 --> 00:02:07,752
Failed,

54
00:02:07,752 --> 00:02:09,056
the pipeline aborts.

55
00:02:09,606 --> 00:02:11,406
So the webhook is the bridge.

56
00:02:11,406 --> 00:02:12,089
Without it,

57
00:02:12,089 --> 00:02:13,330
the wait step waits,

58
00:02:13,330 --> 00:02:14,510
until it times out.

59
00:02:14,510 --> 00:02:15,814
Always add a timeout.

60
00:02:17,364 --> 00:02:18,485
Let us build it.

61
00:02:18,485 --> 00:02:20,027
We sign in to Jenkins.

62
00:02:20,027 --> 00:02:21,078
Manage Jenkins,

63
00:02:21,078 --> 00:02:21,638
Plugins,

64
00:02:21,638 --> 00:02:22,900
Installed plugins.

65
00:02:22,900 --> 00:02:24,301
We search for sonar.

66
00:02:24,301 --> 00:02:27,804
The SonarQube Scanner plugin is already installed.

67
00:02:27,804 --> 00:02:30,327
I installed it before the recording,

68
00:02:30,327 --> 00:02:32,499
from the Jenkins update centre,

69
00:02:32,499 --> 00:02:34,111
then restarted Jenkins.

70
00:02:34,661 --> 00:02:36,578
Now we register the server.

71
00:02:36,578 --> 00:02:37,643
Manage Jenkins,

72
00:02:37,643 --> 00:02:38,495
then System.

73
00:02:38,495 --> 00:02:40,624
We scroll down to the section,

74
00:02:40,624 --> 00:02:41,902
SonarQube servers.

75
00:02:41,902 --> 00:02:43,535
We click Add SonarQube.

76
00:03:02,885 --> 00:03:03,804
Three fields.

77
00:03:03,804 --> 00:03:04,935
The name: sonar.

78
00:03:04,935 --> 00:03:07,692
This is the name the pipeline will use.

79
00:03:07,692 --> 00:03:09,813
The server address: localhost,

80
00:03:09,813 --> 00:03:11,156
port nine thousand.

81
00:03:11,156 --> 00:03:12,145
And the token,

82
00:03:12,145 --> 00:03:14,195
from the Jenkins credentials.

83
00:03:14,195 --> 00:03:15,397
Never typed here.

84
00:03:15,397 --> 00:03:15,963
We save.

85
00:03:22,813 --> 00:03:24,614
Second piece: the webhook.

86
00:03:24,614 --> 00:03:26,346
We sign in to Sonar cube.

87
00:03:26,346 --> 00:03:27,385
Administration,

88
00:03:27,385 --> 00:03:28,355
Configuration,

89
00:03:28,355 --> 00:03:28,979
Webhooks.

90
00:03:28,979 --> 00:03:30,087
We click Create.

91
00:03:39,837 --> 00:03:41,081
The name: jenkins.

92
00:03:41,081 --> 00:03:42,809
The address: our Jenkins,

93
00:03:42,809 --> 00:03:43,224
slash,

94
00:03:43,224 --> 00:03:44,813
sonarqube dash webhook,

95
00:03:44,813 --> 00:03:45,228
slash.

96
00:03:45,228 --> 00:03:47,232
Do not forget the last slash.

97
00:03:47,232 --> 00:03:48,131
We create it.

98
00:03:48,131 --> 00:03:51,379
Now the server knows where to send the verdict.

99
00:03:51,929 --> 00:03:53,880
Third piece: the pipeline file.

100
00:03:53,880 --> 00:03:54,887
In the terminal.

101
00:03:54,887 --> 00:03:56,712
We are in the project folder.

102
00:03:56,712 --> 00:03:58,222
We show the Jenkinsfile.

103
00:03:58,772 --> 00:03:59,682
Three stages.

104
00:03:59,682 --> 00:04:00,732
Build and test,

105
00:04:00,732 --> 00:04:02,481
with the coverage report.

106
00:04:02,481 --> 00:04:02,831
Scan,

107
00:04:02,831 --> 00:04:04,721
inside with Sonar cube env,

108
00:04:04,721 --> 00:04:05,561
named sonar.

109
00:04:05,561 --> 00:04:08,361
And Quality gate: wait for quality gate,

110
00:04:08,361 --> 00:04:09,760
abort pipeline true,

111
00:04:09,760 --> 00:04:12,000
with a timeout of three minutes.

112
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:15,290
The scan line also skips the two browser files,

113
00:04:15,290 --> 00:04:16,969
to keep this demo quick.

114
00:04:17,519 --> 00:04:20,933
The job already exists. We open it, and click Build Now.

115
00:04:26,483 --> 00:04:27,542
Now the console.

116
00:04:27,542 --> 00:04:29,530
Jenkins shows every line live.

117
00:04:29,530 --> 00:04:32,444
Maven builds the project and runs the tests,

118
00:04:32,444 --> 00:04:35,955
and the coverage tool records which lines they touch.

119
00:04:36,505 --> 00:04:37,366
While it runs,

120
00:04:37,366 --> 00:04:39,519
remember the gate from last lesson.

121
00:04:39,519 --> 00:04:42,225
Our project has fifty-nine percent coverage.

122
00:04:42,225 --> 00:04:43,701
The rule says sixty-two.

123
00:04:43,701 --> 00:04:44,931
So this should fail.

124
00:04:45,481 --> 00:04:47,017
Build and test is done,

125
00:04:47,017 --> 00:04:48,552
and all the tests pass.

126
00:04:48,552 --> 00:04:50,088
Next is the Scan stage.

127
00:04:50,088 --> 00:04:52,958
It is the same scan as in the last lessons,

128
00:04:52,958 --> 00:04:54,561
but now Jenkins runs it,

129
00:04:54,561 --> 00:04:58,900
and passes in the address and the token from the server we saved.

130
00:04:59,450 --> 00:05:01,281
No password is typed anywhere.

131
00:05:01,281 --> 00:05:03,905
Jenkins keeps the token in its credentials,

132
00:05:03,905 --> 00:05:06,895
and hands it to the scanner as a hidden variable.

133
00:05:07,445 --> 00:05:09,192
The scanner reads the files,

134
00:05:09,192 --> 00:05:10,190
runs its checks,

135
00:05:10,190 --> 00:05:11,625
and uploads one report.

136
00:05:11,625 --> 00:05:13,933
Then Sonar cube computes the verdict,

137
00:05:13,933 --> 00:05:15,680
and sends it to our webhook.

138
00:05:21,230 --> 00:05:25,987
Failed. The last stage is red. Let us look at the end of the console, to see why.

139
00:05:26,537 --> 00:05:26,889
Here.

140
00:05:26,889 --> 00:05:28,227
The task completed.

141
00:05:28,227 --> 00:05:29,353
Quality gate is,

142
00:05:29,353 --> 00:05:30,057
E R R O R.

143
00:05:30,057 --> 00:05:34,561
And the last line: Pipeline aborted due to quality gate failure.

144
00:05:34,561 --> 00:05:35,828
The build stopped,

145
00:05:35,828 --> 00:05:37,588
because the gate said no.

146
00:05:38,138 --> 00:05:41,594
In Sonar cube, the same story. Quality gate: Failed.

147
00:05:44,644 --> 00:05:45,500
Quick question.

148
00:05:45,500 --> 00:05:48,066
What happens if the webhook address is wrong?

149
00:05:48,066 --> 00:05:48,979
Pause the video,

150
00:05:48,979 --> 00:05:50,063
and think about it.

151
00:06:00,613 --> 00:06:03,808
The answer: Jenkins waits for the full three minutes,

152
00:06:03,808 --> 00:06:05,858
because the verdict never arrives,

153
00:06:05,858 --> 00:06:08,089
and then the timeout stops the build.

154
00:06:08,089 --> 00:06:09,958
That is why we add the timeout.

155
00:06:09,958 --> 00:06:14,842
And abort pipeline true is the part that turns a failed gate into a failed build.

156
00:06:15,392 --> 00:06:16,239
Now we fix it,

157
00:06:16,239 --> 00:06:17,086
the right way,

158
00:06:17,086 --> 00:06:17,751
with tests.

159
00:06:17,751 --> 00:06:19,022
Back in the terminal.

160
00:06:19,022 --> 00:06:21,684
We create a test class for the pricing code,

161
00:06:21,684 --> 00:06:22,288
as before.

162
00:06:22,288 --> 00:06:23,317
And we commit it,

163
00:06:23,317 --> 00:06:23,861
with git.

164
00:06:30,111 --> 00:06:33,525
The commit is in. We go back to the job, and click Build Now.

165
00:06:39,275 --> 00:06:44,267
Again, three stages. The tests now include the new ones, so the coverage goes up.

166
00:06:44,817 --> 00:06:46,550
We watch the console again.

167
00:06:46,550 --> 00:06:47,898
Maven runs the tests,

168
00:06:47,898 --> 00:06:49,695
now with the new test class,

169
00:06:49,695 --> 00:06:52,198
and the coverage report is built again.

170
00:06:52,748 --> 00:06:54,878
Then the scan uploads the new report,

171
00:06:54,878 --> 00:06:58,103
and Sonar cube compares the new coverage with sixty-two.

172
00:06:58,653 --> 00:06:59,823
Another question.

173
00:06:59,823 --> 00:07:01,612
Who decides the sixty-two?

174
00:07:01,612 --> 00:07:02,232
A person,

175
00:07:02,232 --> 00:07:03,196
in Sonar cube,

176
00:07:03,196 --> 00:07:04,228
not in Jenkins.

177
00:07:04,228 --> 00:07:06,568
Jenkins only asks for the verdict,

178
00:07:06,568 --> 00:07:07,463
and obeys it.

179
00:07:08,013 --> 00:07:10,136
Let us recall the three pieces.

180
00:07:10,136 --> 00:07:11,231
One: the server,

181
00:07:11,231 --> 00:07:13,832
saved in Jenkins under the name sonar.

182
00:07:13,832 --> 00:07:14,996
Two: the webhook,

183
00:07:14,996 --> 00:07:15,954
in Sonar cube,

184
00:07:15,954 --> 00:07:17,666
pointing back to Jenkins.

185
00:07:17,666 --> 00:07:19,035
Three: the pipeline,

186
00:07:19,035 --> 00:07:21,773
with the scan and the wait for the gate.

187
00:07:26,323 --> 00:07:30,291
Green. All three stages. The gate passed, and the pipeline went on.

188
00:07:30,841 --> 00:07:32,804
Notice what we did not change.

189
00:07:32,804 --> 00:07:33,590
Not Jenkins,

190
00:07:33,590 --> 00:07:34,571
not Sonar cube.

191
00:07:34,571 --> 00:07:35,487
Only the code.

192
00:07:35,487 --> 00:07:38,039
The gate and the pipeline are the same.

193
00:07:38,039 --> 00:07:43,667
That is the point of putting the gate in the pipeline: the rule is applied every time,

194
00:07:43,667 --> 00:07:45,433
and nobody has to remember.

195
00:07:45,983 --> 00:07:49,823
The console agrees. Quality gate is, O K. Finished: success.

196
00:07:51,573 --> 00:07:52,584
In a real team,

197
00:07:52,584 --> 00:07:56,355
a red build like the first one would also notify people,

198
00:07:56,355 --> 00:07:57,501
by email or chat.

199
00:07:57,501 --> 00:07:59,993
The developer sees it within minutes,

200
00:07:59,993 --> 00:08:02,283
and fixes it before anyone merges.

201
00:08:02,833 --> 00:08:05,585
Finally, the proof. Lab check. Four of four.

202
00:08:06,135 --> 00:08:07,156
Jenkins answers.

203
00:08:07,156 --> 00:08:08,368
The webhook exists.

204
00:08:08,368 --> 00:08:10,282
The build waited for the gate.

205
00:08:10,282 --> 00:08:11,558
And the gate passed.

206
00:08:11,558 --> 00:08:13,217
The results are in a file.

207
00:08:14,767 --> 00:08:15,919
Five mistakes.

208
00:08:16,469 --> 00:08:18,172
One: forgetting the webhook.

209
00:08:18,172 --> 00:08:19,328
The pipeline hangs,

210
00:08:19,328 --> 00:08:20,423
until the timeout.

211
00:08:20,423 --> 00:08:21,153
If it hangs,

212
00:08:21,153 --> 00:08:22,613
check the webhook first.

213
00:08:23,163 --> 00:08:25,056
Two: a wrong webhook address.

214
00:08:25,056 --> 00:08:26,948
Missing the slash at the end,

215
00:08:26,948 --> 00:08:28,123
or the wrong port.

216
00:08:28,123 --> 00:08:30,407
Sonar cube shows the last delivery,

217
00:08:30,407 --> 00:08:31,452
with its status.

218
00:08:31,452 --> 00:08:31,974
Read it.

219
00:08:32,524 --> 00:08:38,070
Three: no timeout. A lost webhook means a build that waits for ever, and blocks an agent.

220
00:08:38,620 --> 00:08:43,954
Four: putting the token in the Jenkinsfile. Use the credential, in the Jenkins settings.

221
00:08:44,504 --> 00:08:47,793
Five: the wait step in the same stage as the scan,

222
00:08:47,793 --> 00:08:50,753
holding a build agent while the server works.

223
00:08:50,753 --> 00:08:51,739
Fine for a lab.

224
00:08:51,739 --> 00:08:52,857
In a busy system,

225
00:08:52,857 --> 00:08:54,436
wait on the server side,

226
00:08:54,436 --> 00:08:55,554
without an agent.

227
00:08:57,104 --> 00:08:59,899
Where to find the lab. Pause here, and write it down.

228
00:09:00,449 --> 00:09:01,913
One: the repository,

229
00:09:01,913 --> 00:09:06,233
git hub dot com slash it dash waves slash dev ops dash A I,

230
00:09:06,233 --> 00:09:08,577
in the folder academy slash lab.

231
00:09:09,127 --> 00:09:15,271
Two: the files, lab one sixty-nine dot S H, and shortcuts one sixty-nine dot S H.

232
00:09:15,821 --> 00:09:17,647
Three: load the short names,

233
00:09:17,647 --> 00:09:20,582
with source shortcuts one sixty-nine dot S H.

234
00:09:20,582 --> 00:09:22,669
Then lab check tests your setup.

235
00:09:23,219 --> 00:09:24,803
Four: set Jenkins auth,

236
00:09:24,803 --> 00:09:25,904
and Sonar token,

237
00:09:25,904 --> 00:09:26,800
as variables,

238
00:09:26,800 --> 00:09:28,108
to your own values.

239
00:09:28,108 --> 00:09:31,069
Never put them in a file in the repository.

240
00:09:31,619 --> 00:09:33,178
Five: install the plugin,

241
00:09:33,178 --> 00:09:34,424
register the server,

242
00:09:34,424 --> 00:09:35,421
add the webhook,

243
00:09:35,421 --> 00:09:36,045
and build.

244
00:09:36,045 --> 00:09:36,855
Make it fail,

245
00:09:36,855 --> 00:09:37,977
then make it pass.

246
00:09:38,527 --> 00:09:40,169
The link is in the description.

247
00:09:41,719 --> 00:09:42,594
Your turn.

248
00:09:43,144 --> 00:09:48,477
One: install the SonarQube Scanner plugin in your Jenkins, and register your server.

249
00:09:49,027 --> 00:09:52,590
Two: add the webhook in Sonar cube, with the slash at the end.

250
00:09:53,140 --> 00:09:58,217
Three: add the two stages to your Jenkinsfile, and run it. Does the gate stop the build?

251
00:09:58,767 --> 00:10:02,116
Four: fix the code, and run it again, until it is green.

252
00:10:02,666 --> 00:10:05,312
Five: run lab check, and get four of four.

253
00:10:05,862 --> 00:10:07,590
Pause the video, and do it now.

254
00:10:23,140 --> 00:10:24,015
Quick check.

255
00:10:24,565 --> 00:10:25,930
What does the webhook do?

256
00:10:26,480 --> 00:10:28,037
What happens if it is missing?

257
00:10:28,587 --> 00:10:30,699
Why use a timeout around the wait step?

258
00:10:31,249 --> 00:10:32,636
Where does the token live?

259
00:10:33,186 --> 00:10:39,053
Objective covered: M C eighteen, objective six. Scanning and the gate in a pipeline.

260
00:10:39,603 --> 00:10:41,672
Pause the video, and answer out loud.

261
00:10:52,222 --> 00:10:56,638
Next: tokens and permissions, who may scan, and who may change the gate.

262
00:10:57,188 --> 00:11:00,516
If this helped, like, share and subscribe, so you do not miss it.
